    {
      "id": "116",
      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 116,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "The へ in both patterns is the same directional particle. While it's commonly used with いく to indicate going somewhere or moving in a direction (e.g., 学校へいく, 西へいく), it can also be used with other verbs (e.g., 家へ帰る, 公園へ歩く) or in certain phrases (e.g., 東京へようこそ！). In all cases, へ expresses directionality or movement toward a location.",
        "first_relatable": {
          "id": 38,
          "slug": "へ",
          "title": "へ",
          "meaning": "To, Toward",
          "level": "JLPT5",
          "type_pascal": "GrammarPoint",
          "type_snake": "grammar_point"
        },
        "second_relatable": {
