    },
    {
      "id": "117",
      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 117,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "The particle へ indicates direction or destination, similar to 'to' or 'toward' in English. に向かって and に向けて emphasize direction rather than destination, unlike へ, which can also imply the final goal. For example, 学校へ行く means 'go to school,' while 学校に向かって走る means 'run toward the school.'",
        "first_relatable": {
          "id": 38,
